<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>WorldCover + canopy height trial</title><style>
*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;background:#f2f4ef;color:#203b40;font:14px system-ui,sans-serif}main{max-width:1400px;margin:auto;padding:28px}h1{font-size:29px;margin:8px 0}h2{font-size:19px}p{line-height:1.55;max-width:1040px}.small{font-size:12px;color:#536d70}.controls,.legend{display:flex;gap:20px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin:20px 0}label{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:7px}select{padding:8px;font:14px system-ui;color:#203b40;border:1px solid #bccdc7;border-radius:6px;background:white}.panels{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:16px}.panel{background:white;border:1px solid #cedad4;border-radius:10px;padding:14px}canvas{width:100%;aspect-ratio:1;background:#e2edf0}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}td,th{padding:8px;border-bottom:1px solid #d3ddd8;text-align:left}th{font-size:12px}section{margin:28px 0}.scroll{overflow:auto}.note{padding:14px;background:#e7ede3;border-radius:8px}a{color:#146f72}pre{font-size:11px;white-space:pre-wrap;max-height:350px;overflow:auto}summary{cursor:pointer}.swatch{display:inline-block;width:13px;height:13px;margin-right:6px}.hatched{background:repeating-linear-gradient(45deg,#b8c7c1 0 3px,#fff 3px 5px)}@media(max-width:850px){main{padding:16px}.panels{grid-template-columns:1fr}h1{font-size:23px}}
</style></head><body><main>
<p class="small">Bounded research trial · Dungeness and Sequim · 2020 vegetation inputs</p><h1>WorldCover classes + canopy height</h1>
<p>This trial estimates how vegetation reduces an otherwise visible view. Terrain and buildings establish the baseline. WorldCover identifies the vegetation class, canopy height defines the modeled column, and a class-specific attenuation rule reduces support only along ray segments inside that column. The resulting <strong>modeled transmission support</strong> averages all observer/target-water comparisons. It is an assumption-based estimate, with no calibrated detection probability.</p>
<p class="note">The central attenuation setting reuses the historical OrcaCast coefficient, with weaker and stronger scenarios available below. The main trial assumes zero vegetation where WorldCover reports water and canopy height is missing. The strict comparison preserves those unknowns. Missing land canopy height or intersected missing classes retain a range and an unavailable complete score. The original canopy envelope is shown alongside the estimate.</p>
<div class="controls"><label>Site<select id="site"></select></label><label>Viewpoints<select id="profile"><option value="fast">Land-cell average · fast sampling</option><option value="fast_strict">Land-cell average · strict missing heights</option><option value="reference">Land-cell average · full target reference</option><option value="exact_point">Historical exact shoreline viewpoint</option></select></label><label>Vegetation attenuation<select id="beta"></select></label></div>
<p id="summary"></p><div class="legend"><span><i class="swatch" style="background:#bd725c"></i>0 support</span><span><i class="swatch" style="background:#187d75"></i>1 support</span><span><i class="swatch hatched"></i>Input uncertainty · lower bound shown</span><span>✚ Land observers · amber dot: historical viewpoint</span></div>
<div class="panels"><div class="panel"><h2>Terrain + buildings</h2><p class="small">Baseline geometric visibility fraction</p><canvas id="baseline" role="img" aria-label="Terrain and building baseline"></canvas></div><div class="panel"><h2>Vegetation-adjusted estimate</h2><p class="small">Modeled transmission support · bounds if inputs are missing</p><canvas id="modeled" role="img" aria-label="Classified canopy modeled support"></canvas></div><div class="panel"><h2>WorldCover classes</h2><p class="small">Nearest categorical alignment · 10 m calculation grid</p><canvas id="classes" role="img" aria-label="WorldCover land cover map"></canvas></div></div>
<div id="classes-legend" class="legend small"></div>
<section><h2>Scores on the same water-cell populations</h2><div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Target cell</th><th>Terrain + buildings</th><th>Canopy envelope bounds</th><th>Modeled score</th><th>Modeled bounds</th><th>Missing-input comparisons</th></tr></thead><tbody id="pairs"></tbody></table></div></section>
<section><h2>Runtime and target-sampling agreement</h2><p class="small">Measured warm calculation includes terrain/building rays, private canopy clearance, all three attenuation scenarios and cell aggregation. WorldCover alignment, loading and compilation warmup are separate. Differences compare fast sampling with all retained water targets, using the same 15 observers and model assumptions.</p><div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Site</th><th>Full target reference</th><th>Fast sampling</th><th>Speedup</th><th>Maximum difference</th><th>Sampling agreement</th></tr></thead><tbody id="runtime"></tbody></table></div></section>
<section><h2>What the model assumes</h2><p>The attenuation coefficient is 0.002 per weighted metre in the central scenario. Its class-height coefficients reuse the old OrcaCast defaults: canopy heights below 2 m, 2–5 m, 5–15 m and at least 15 m receive obstruction levels 0, 0.25, 0.65 and 1. The class multiplier and floor then modify that level. Floors never invent vegetation height: zero-height columns and rays above the canopy remain unattenuated. Terrain and roofs remain opaque in their separate baseline.</p><p>A ray crossing 100 weighted metres retains about 82% transmission in the central scenario. This is an illustrative model rule, not measured tree transparency. Ground-to-canopy-top columns do not describe actual crown bases, trunks or undergrowth. WorldCover water with a positive canopy height remains a conflict. Missing height remains unknown for built-up, grass, tree and other land classes. Only missing zero-floor canopy in WorldCover water is resolved as zero vegetation in the main trial; the strict comparison retains the original missingness. This classification assumption does not change terrain, buildings, water-target geometry or the original canopy mask. The 30 m canopy clearance around each observer is a retained assumption; it leaves neighboring roofs intact.</p>
<div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>WorldCover class</th><th>Height obstruction multiplier</th><th>Obstruction floor</th></tr></thead><tbody id="coefficients"></tbody></table></div></section>
<section><h2>Source-cell vegetation context</h2><p class="small">Class proportions below use 10 m grid centres inside the source land geometry, excluding rasterized roofs. They describe vegetation context and do not weight observer access or sampling.</p><div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Class</th><th>Dungeness outdoor land</th><th>Sequim outdoor land</th></tr></thead><tbody id="source-classes"></tbody></table></div></section>
<section><h2>Scope and provenance</h2><p>Two source cells and 18 complete retained raster-water target cells within the original 5 km windows. Terrain retains 30 m support; canopy and WorldCover use 2020 inputs. Building inventory is assumed complete. The observer design, target populations, curvature and source grounding match the saved benchmark. This trial does not establish field accuracy or observer-sampling convergence, and is separate from the canonical production kernel.</p><p id="lookup"></p><p><a href="worldcover_view_scores.parquet">Selected cell-to-cell lookup</a> · <a href="worldcover_canopy_scores.parquet">All scenarios and viewpoint scores</a> · <a href="report.json">Complete model and provenance</a></p><p class="small">© ESA WorldCover project 2020 / Contains modified Copernicus Sentinel data (2020) processed by ESA WorldCover consortium · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://esa-worldcover.org/en/data-access">WorldCover documentation</a></p><details><summary>Input hashes, parameters and preparation timings</summary><pre id="provenance"></pre></details></section>
</main><script id="payload" type="application/json">__PAYLOAD__</script><script>
(()=>{'use strict';const D=JSON.parse(document.getElementById('payload').textContent),el=id=>document.getElementById(id),fmt=x=>x===null?'Unavailable':x.toFixed(3),colors={0:'#ad9abc',10:'#35734e',20:'#9a9b4d',30:'#c4d08a',40:'#dfbb67',50:'#bf7868',60:'#d6ccba',70:'#fafafa',80:'#b1d5e1',90:'#78a89b',95:'#20715a',100:'#b7bc8b'},name=k=>D.model.classes[k]?.class_name||'Missing class';let site,images={};
for(const s of D.sites){let o=document.createElement('option');o.value=s.name;o.textContent=s.name;el('site').append(o);const im=new Image();im.onload=()=>render();im.src=s.worldcover_png;images[s.name]=im}for(const b of D.model.beta_per_m){let o=document.createElement('option');o.value=b;o.textContent=b===0.002?'Central · 0.002 /m':b<0.002?'Weaker attenuation · '+b+' /m':'Stronger attenuation · '+b+' /m';el('beta').append(o)}el('beta').value=D.model.default_beta_per_m;el('profile').value=D.selected_profile;
const selected=()=>D.pairs.filter(r=>r.site===site.name&&r.profile===el('profile').value&&r.beta_per_m===Number(el('beta').value));function polygon(ctx,points,point){ctx.beginPath();points.forEach((p,i)=>{let q=point(p);i?ctx.lineTo(...q):ctx.moveTo(...q)});ctx.closePath()}function geometry(ctx,g,point){const polys=g.type==='Polygon'?[g.coordinates]:g.type==='MultiPolygon'?g.coordinates:[];ctx.beginPath();for(const p of polys)for(const ring of p){ring.forEach((v,i)=>{let q=point(v);i?ctx.lineTo(...q):ctx.moveTo(...q)});ctx.closePath()}}
function draw(id){const c=el(id),w=c.getBoundingClientRect().width,ratio=devicePixelRatio||1;c.width=w*ratio;c.height=w*ratio;const ctx=c.getContext('2d');ctx.scale(ratio,ratio);const coords=Object.values(site.target_polygons).flat().concat(site.observers.map(p=>p.slice(0,2))),xs=coords.map(p=>p[0]),ys=coords.map(p=>p[1]),cx=(Math.min(...xs)+Math.max(...xs))/2,cy=(Math.min(...ys)+Math.max(...ys))/2,scale=w/Math.max(Math.max(...xs)-Math.min(...xs)+800,Math.max(...ys)-Math.min(...ys)+800),point=p=>[w/2+(p[0]-cx)*scale,w/2-(p[1]-cy)*scale];ctx.fillStyle='#e2edf0';ctx.fillRect(0,0,w,w);geometry(ctx,site.metadata.land,point);ctx.fillStyle='#eceee4';ctx.fill('evenodd');if(id==='classes'){const t=site.grid.transform,sh=site.grid.shape,a=point([t[2],t[5]]),b=point([t[2]+sh[1]*t[0],t[5]+sh[0]*t[4]]);ctx.imageSmoothingEnabled=false;if(images[site.name].complete)ctx.drawImage(images[site.name],a[0],a[1],b[0]-a[0],b[1]-a[1])}else for(const r of selected()){const value=id==='baseline'?r.terrain_building_lower:r.modeled_lower,missing=id==='baseline'?r.terrain_building_score===null:r.modeled_score===null;polygon(ctx,site.target_polygons[r.target_h3],point);ctx.fillStyle=`rgb(${Math.round(189-165*value)},${Math.round(114+11*value)},${Math.round(92+25*value)})`;ctx.fill();if(missing){ctx.save();ctx.clip();ctx.strokeStyle='#fff';ctx.lineWidth=1;for(let x=-w;x<2*w;x+=8){ctx.beginPath();ctx.moveTo(x,0);ctx.lineTo(x-w,w);ctx.stroke()}ctx.restore()}ctx.strokeStyle='#fff';ctx.lineWidth=1;ctx.stroke()}geometry(ctx,site.metadata.source_land,point);ctx.strokeStyle='#203b40';ctx.lineWidth=2;ctx.stroke();let points=el('profile').value==='exact_point'?[]:site.observers;for(const p of points){let [x,y]=point(p);ctx.beginPath();ctx.moveTo(x-3,y);ctx.lineTo(x+3,y);ctx.moveTo(x,y-3);ctx.lineTo(x,y+3);ctx.stroke()}let [x,y]=point(site.exact_point);ctx.fillStyle='#c38636';ctx.beginPath();ctx.arc(x,y,4,0,2*Math.PI);ctx.fill();ctx.font='11px system-ui';ctx.fillStyle='#203b40';ctx.fillText('↑ N · '+site.source_h3,8,17)}
function render(){site=D.sites.find(s=>s.name===el('site').value);if(!site)return;const rows=selected(),total=rows.reduce((a,r)=>a+r.target_population_count,0),mean=f=>rows.reduce((a,r)=>a+r[f]*r.target_population_count,0)/total,unknown=mean('input_unknown_fraction');el('summary').textContent=site.name+': terrain/building support '+(100*mean('terrain_building_lower')).toFixed(1)+'–'+(100*mean('terrain_building_upper')).toFixed(1)+'%; vegetation-adjusted modeled support '+(100*mean('modeled_lower')).toFixed(1)+'–'+(100*mean('modeled_upper')).toFixed(1)+'%. Missing-input comparisons: '+(100*unknown).toFixed(1)+'%. This averages the retained target-water area for the selected viewpoints.';el('pairs').innerHTML=rows.map(r=>`<tr><td>${r.target_h3}</td><td>${fmt(r.terrain_building_score)}</td><td>${fmt(r.canopy_envelope_lower)} – ${fmt(r.canopy_envelope_upper)}</td><td>${fmt(r.modeled_score)}</td><td>${fmt(r.modeled_lower)} – ${fmt(r.modeled_upper)}</td><td>${(100*r.input_unknown_fraction).toFixed(1)}%</td></tr>`).join('');for(const id of ['baseline','modeled','classes'])draw(id)}
el('runtime').innerHTML=D.sites.map(s=>{const r=s.profiles.reference,f=s.profiles.fast;return `<tr><td>${s.name}</td><td>${r.median_seconds.toFixed(3)} s</td><td>${f.median_seconds.toFixed(3)} s</td><td>${(r.median_seconds/f.median_seconds).toFixed(1)}×</td><td>${(100*f.errors.maximum).toFixed(2)} percentage points</td><td>${f.accepted?'Pass':'Fail; lookup uses reference'}</td></tr>`}).join('');el('coefficients').innerHTML=Object.entries(D.model.classes).map(([k,v])=>`<tr><td>${k} · ${v.class_name}</td><td>${v.obstruction_multiplier.toFixed(2)}</td><td>${v.obstruction_floor.toFixed(2)}</td></tr>`).join('');el('classes-legend').innerHTML=Object.keys(colors).map(k=>`<span><i class="swatch" style="background:${colors[k]}"></i>${name(k)}</span>`).join('');el('source-classes').innerHTML=Object.keys(colors).map(k=>'<tr><td>'+name(k)+'</td>'+D.sites.map(s=>{const total=Object.values(s.source_class_counts).reduce((a,b)=>a+b,0);return '<td>'+(100*(s.source_class_counts[k]||0)/total).toFixed(1)+'%</td>'}).join('')+'</tr>').join('');el('lookup').textContent='The saved lookup uses '+D.selected_profile+' sampling at the central attenuation setting. Reading it and selecting one source took '+(1000*D.median_disk_lookup_seconds).toFixed(1)+' ms on this machine.';el('provenance').textContent=JSON.stringify({scientific_signature:D.scientific_signature,model:D.model,worldcover:D.worldcover,prepared_checksums:D.prepared_checksums,benchmark_sha256:D.benchmark_sha256,sites:D.sites.map(s=>({site:s.name,preparation_seconds:s.preparation_seconds,warmup_seconds:s.warmup_seconds,grid:s.grid,observer_classes:s.observer_classes,missing_height_class_counts:s.missing_height_class_counts,water_class_resolved_pixels:s.water_class_resolved_pixels}))},null,2);for(const id of ['site','profile','beta'])el(id).onchange=render;new ResizeObserver(render).observe(document.querySelector('.panels'));render()})();
</script></body></html>
